    "rating": 4.1,
    "reference": "ChIJRcCJkj1IyUwRGO7EqlWAa7A",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Kelli Chouinard",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103090908512058343442/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKVVzYHyugUGNCqrzIYTM2p-PcUzMMWyWAvxOOYF69TEr1_1w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
        "text": "Really great service from start to finish! I called only 20 minutes before and they were kind enough to fit me in. Such a welcoming experience, and Lynda was fantastic—absolutely loved her. Will definitely be back!",
        "time": 1767392967,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Tushita Paul",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117793429082082551559/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXXI-tXFmBHxlihjlPv1gA1cGBxngnlWdivTEhP0gTDWDO98fIzvw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "7 months ago",
        "text": "Worst experience ever at a nail salon.\n\nI had a 10:30 am appointment but was only attended to at 11:15, and not once did the owner apologize for the delay. What’s the point of booking an appointment if they accept walk-ins and keep you waiting who had an appointment ?\n\nThe male nail tech was unprofessional and distracted, looking everywhere while working, and eventually ended up HURTING my pinkie while filing. He FORGOT to remove product from the acrylic on my fingertips that I had to remove back home. He FORGOT to put cuticle oil, didn’t shape my nails correctly and when I asked him to fix it, he started huffing and puffing, clearly annoyed. It was clear he was rushing because they had entertained walk-ins during my appointment time, and now he was late for his lunch.\n\nI also got a regular pedicure, which was a complete joke for $45. It was just a soak, less than 30 seconds of scrubbing, a quick polish, and they FORGOT to apply moisturizer!!!!!!!!!\n\nI only realized this when it was time to pay, but by then I just didn’t care.\n\nTheir name is a joke because both my sister and I left unhappy that day. She faced the same problems that I did and she was a regular there. She got nicked on her pinkie too and the nail color was damaged on the left ring finger but the male nail tech didn’t care. He was running late for lunch as I mentioned.\n\nOverall, the staff was rude, rushed, and careless, and the service quality did not match the price at all. We will never return and would not recommend this place to anyone looking for a professional, relaxing nail salon experience.",
        "time": 1751159903,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Adriana Maldonado",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101551938274674977930/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVebhM_bePhEtEr0qTSOTKqF3qAXAQl9gY_0DeYFJd6TL6VNi7v=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "8 months ago",
        "text": "I was looking for a place for a manicure and pedicure, as soon as I got there I felt relaxed with the music and the display of beautiful beaches on a tv screen, my pedicure was amazing, very clean and so well done!\nMy nails perfectly done too even though I came close to the closing time, so I recommend to make your appointment way before. I appreciate they took me without an appointment and made the time for me. 🙏🏻 + they’re celebrating their 21 years in business and gave lovely and special goodies to the clients!\nI’m definitely come back every 3 weeks! 🤩",
        "time": 1749418915,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Gurwinder Kaur",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/104677388671276540941/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocI2JzXxu5tnoRjv6ETjUg7oXean62BYQez2X3dVOxEoKQ8SsRj5=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "5 months ago",
        "text": "Very disappointing….. I asked for shellac hand and feet nails. And I am coming here from last two years, I always ask them the same. And when I arrive there they ask ok long nails or just shellac on your own nails. It has been simple for a year.\n\nBut today the only man who works there, was so arrogant and his tone was so rough; Said, I don’t have time to do your long nails, because you asked for Shellac only. Like seriously, I am coming here for more than a year now, asking same thing when I book an appointment. Lady who did my manicure, took 1.30 minutes just to do my feet. I have a party tomorrow, and it’s already 5:30PM. Where should do my nails now.\nAbove that, he said you came 5 minutes late so that’s why I have no time. But it’s not my fault if you are asking client to sit for extra 15-20 minutes because you are doing somebody nails. Then after doing pedicure, you say that I don’t have tym to do your hands. This is my last tym visiting this arrogant place who don’t know how to talk their customers. Well congratulations for spoiling somebody baby shower and Bd’y party double event. Here are the hands, I will have tomorrow in big event.",
        "time": 1756502766,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Kaylie Owen",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101299190863321095241/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUDocB-WI9LQ2NrWwAx04bILEVYCHcEd3x3izjW-yPa-0m18SWx=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
